            <ArticleTitle>Electric heating pad burns.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>819-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with sensory deficits are especially prone to heating pad burns. Two cases are reported of patients with anesthetic skin who received partial and full-thickness burns of their feet from an electric heating pad. These burn injuries could have been prevented if the patients understood the potential hazard of heating pads.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
